   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to allowing the use of rifles for hunting in the county of Madison; and providing for the repeal of such provisions upon the expiration thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S5082",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5082-2011",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §11-0907, En Con L",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5082\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to allowing the\nuse of rifles for hunting in the county of Madison; and providing\nfor the\nrepeal of such provisions upon the expiration thereof\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\nThis bill would allow the hunting of deer through the use of a rifle in\nMadison County as well as provide for a coextensive sunset of the\nprovisions of this subdivision.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nThe conservation clubs of Madison County have requested that that County\nbe included in those areas where sportsmen and women are able to hunt\ndeer with rifles. Since 2005, several counties in Southern and Central\nNew York have been allowing the hunting of deer and bear with rifles\nwith few if any reported incidents or other problems. With that safe\nhistory, it would seem to only make sense to now include Madison County\nwithin these provisions.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY: Chapter 412 of the Laws of\n2008\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS: None\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nImmediately, with provisions\n\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "printNo": "S5082",
    "publishDate": "2011-05-03",
